{"reply":"You can acknowledge the effort without treating it as a reason to give up your voice. For example:

> “I appreciate how much you’ve been carrying and the work you’ve put into moving this forward. I also want to understand the reversal and have a chance to share concerns before the next decision. Could we set aside time to revisit the plan together? I’m not questioning your commitment—I’m asking to be part of the discussion and understand how we’re deciding.”

Keeping the focus on the process—what changed, how decisions are made, and when the team can weigh in—helps you speak up without judging their character. You can also ask a concrete question such as, “What input would be useful from me before we finalize this?”","memory":{"kind":"no_memory_candidate","reason_code":"automatic_capture_disabled"}}
